## Language by layer

Match the layer you are in, not a preference. Harbor's security floor is pure POSIX `sh`;
its trio is Python; vendored skill-tools are TypeScript on Bun. This project's tests are
POSIX `sh` (`tests/`), so they run on any laptop with no install. Code under test keeps
the language of the layer it belongs to.

## Tests

- `sh tests/run.sh` — the runner: every suite in `tests/suites.txt`, then one summary line.
- `tests/lib/core.sh` — harbor's own suite harness, copied: `t_init`, `t_section`, `t_eq`, `t_has`, `t_exit`, `t_done`.
- One suite per unit: `tests/<unit>/<unit>.test.sh`. Add it to `tests/suites.txt`; an unlisted suite is red.
- Red first: write the test, watch it fail, then make it pass. A test that cannot fail does not count.
- `tests/example/example.test.sh` is the worked example; replace it when the first real suite exists.

## Memory

Sessions in this project load the box's memory store: `harbor hub project register` routed it.
Nothing is stored in this repository.

